answer_text:
Under the Public Health Service Act, 2075 (2018), the following rights and guarantees are explicitly provided:

* **Implementation of constitutional rights:** The Act is enacted to implement the right to get free basic health service and emergency health service guaranteed by the Constitution of Nepal, and to establish citizens' access to regular, effective, qualitative, and easily available health service [E1].
* **Right to quality health service:** Every citizen has the right to obtain quality health service in an easy and convenient manner [E2].
* **Protection from deprivation of health service:** No citizen shall be deprived of health service [E2], [E3].
* **Right to free basic health services:** Every citizen has the right to obtain free basic health services under the following prescribed headings [E2], [E3]:
  * Vaccination service [E2], [E3];
  * Motherhood, infant, and pediatric health service (such as integrated infant and pediatric disease management, nutrition service, pregnancy, labor and child birth service, family planning, abortion, and reproductive health) [E2], [E3];
  * Service relating to communicable disease [E2], [E3];
  * Service relating to non-communicable disease and physical disability [E2], [E3];
  * Service relating to mental disease [E2], [E3];
  * Service relating to elderly citizen's health [E2], [E3];
  * Service of general emergency condition [E2], [E3];
  * Ayurveda and other accredited alternative health service [E3]; and
  * Other services prescribed by the Government of Nepal by a notification in the Nepal Gazette [E3].

